/// @namespace dannan
/// Dannan: the network layer a cluster's hosted systems run on. dannan::Node is a node, and
/// dannan::Context what a hosted system sees of it.

/// @namespace dannan::contract
/// The stack's shared vocabulary: the clocks (TimeSource, WallClock), waits on them (TimeWait),
/// completions, Outcome and Fault, and the thread-safety annotations.

/// @namespace dannan::identity
/// Who a node is and what it holds secret: node ids, keys and custody, certificates, and the
/// cryptographic helpers every project shares (Argon2id, stored passwords, AES-GCM).

/// @namespace dannan::net
/// The transport: sessions and lanes, calls and replies, the request scheduler, and channels
/// (Fanout) with their delivery kinds.

/// @namespace dannan::listen
/// The public side: listeners for a hosted system's own clients, their TLS, and the limits on
/// callers (RateLimiter, Backoff).

/// @namespace dannan::sched
/// Scheduling work and memory by class: the retained-memory ledger, the class gates, the worker
/// pool, and the transfer-buffer pool.

/// @namespace dannan::status
/// What a node says about itself: logging, telemetry, readiness and health.

/// @namespace dannan::supervise
/// Running things: supervised threads, the process runner, and the node-program helper a node
/// binary's main is made of.

/// @namespace dannan::config
/// The configuration reader every node binary shares, and the node settings under cluster.*.
